r be returned); no test covers the bypass scenario; and the run_enable_case helper function (lines 146-195 of the test file) is defined but never called and directly references enable-required-check.sh, a clear extras-carve-out AC violation. One nit: the scaffolder's first denylist case block is a strict subset of the second case block and is dead code.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CORR-CRIT-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"CRIT\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"dispatch_note_mode regex allows leading whitespace (^[ \\\\\\\\t]*cascade-status:), while cascade_status uses strict ^cascade-status:. A DISPATCH-NOTE with '  cascade-status: not applicable' (indented) before 'cascade-status: onboarded' sets dispatch_note_mode='not applicable' → exit 0, skipping the cascade_status check entirely. All enforcement (log-entry check, target-match, TF-row regex, negative log-modification assertion) is bypassed.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:121 — re.search(r'(?m)^[ \\\\\\\\t]*cascade-status:\\\\\\\\s+([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]+?)\\\\\\\\s*$', text). Lines 133-136: if [ \\\\\\\"$dispatch_note_mode\\\\\\\" = \\\\\\\"not applicable\\\\\\\" ]; then exit 0; fi fires before cascade_status is parsed. Line 145 re.findall(r'^cascade-status:...') is never reached in the bypass path. No test exercises the indented-not-applicable-before-onboarded case.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Fail-closed contract violated. Any real cascade slice DISPATCH-NOTE can be modified with one indented leading line ('  cascade-status: not applicable') to exit 0 without verifying the branch-protection log, target match, TF-row format, or log-not-modified assertion — defeating all four invariant-2 enforcement paths simultaneously.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Remove '[ \\\\\\\\t]*' from the dispatch_note_mode regex at line 121: change r'(?m)^[ \\\\\\\\t]*cascade-status:\\\\\\\\s+([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]+?)\\\\\\\\s*$' to r'(?m)^cascade-status:\\\\\\\\s+([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]+?)\\\\\\\\s*$'. This makes both parsers require strict line-start, closing the bypass while preserving correct behavior for standard non-indented declarations.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CORR-MAJ-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The case statement branch 'not applicable') at lines 156-160 of check-invocation-log-entry.sh is unreachable dead code. cascade_status uses re.findall(r'^cascade-status:\\\\\\\\s+([a-z-]+)\\\\\\\\s*$', ...) where [a-z-]+ excludes spaces; 'not applicable' contains a space and can never be returned. The branch creates false confidence that 'not applicable' is handled in two places.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:145 — ([a-z-]+) captures only chars in [a-z-]; space is excluded. For 'cascade-status: not applicable', ([a-z-]+) matches 'not' then \\\\\\\\s*$ fails at ' applicable'. findall returns []. Lines 156-160: '\\\\\\\"not applicable\\\\\\\"') branch can never be entered. dispatch_note_mode (line 121) is the sole handler.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"If dispatch_note_mode is ever refactored away (e.g., to unify the two passes), 'cascade-status: not applicable' falls through to FAIL-CLOSED with a misleading error rather than being caught by the supposedly second handler. Dead code also masks the design gap to code reviewers.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Remove the unreachable '\\\\\\\"not applicable\\\\\\\"') case branch (lines 156-160). Alternatively, fix cascade_status regex to also capture 'not applicable' (e.g., replace ([a-z-]+) with ([a-z][a-z -]*)) so the case branch becomes reachable, and document dispatch_note_mode as the primary early-exit handler.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CORR-MAJ-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"run_enable_case function (lines 146-195) is defined but never called in main(), and directly invokes $REPO_ROOT/scripts/enable-required-check.sh at line 157. DISPATCH-NOTE acceptance criteria explicitly requires 'no enable-required-check.sh references in test bodies'. This is residual content from the extras-