\\\\\\s+([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]+?)\\\\\\\\s*$' to r'(?m)^cascade-status:\\\\\\\\s+([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]+?)\\\\\\\\s*$'. Both passes then share the same strict line-start anchor. Alternatively, remove the first pass entirely and handle not-applicable as a recognised value in the second-pass case statement (requires fixing SBP-MAJ-002 first).\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SBP-MAJ-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"When --branch-protection-log is given as an absolute path with --diff-base, normalize_path (os.path.normpath, line 103) keeps the value absolute; git diff --name-only at line 187 returns repo-relative paths; grep -Fxq at line 192 never matches → branch_log_modified=0 always. For blocked-on-adopter-conflict, the log-not-modified assertion silently passes even when the log was actually modified.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:103 normalize_path = os.path.normpath (not relative-ised). Line 187: git diff --name-only returns 'docs/reviews/.../branch-protection-log.md'. Line 192: grep -Fxq '/abs/path/.../branch-protection-log.md' fails against relative entry → branch_log_modified=0. Test case 18 uses a double-slash path (stays relative after normpath) and passes, masking the absolute-path variant.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"blocked-on-adopter-conflict negative assertion (log NOT modified) passes falsely when log was modified, because branch_log_modified=0. Attacker declares conflict-close while actually invoking enable-required-check.sh and modifying the log; CI passes. Requires passing --branch-protection-log as an absolute path — unusual but undocumented as invalid input.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Compute the log path relative to REPO_ROOT before the grep comparison: relpath=\\\\\\\"${BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG_REAL#${REPO_ROOT}/}\\\\\\\"; grep -Fxq \\\\\\\"$relpath\\\\\\\" <<<\\\\\\\"$changed_files\\\\\\\". Alternatively, reject absolute --branch-protection-log values outright, since git diff --name-only always returns repo-relative paths.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SBP-MAJ-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The 'not applicable') case branch at lines 157-160 in case \\\\\\\"$cascade_status\\\\\\\" is unreachable dead code. Second-pass regex ([a-z-]+) at line 145 cannot capture strings containing spaces; 'not applicable' can never be assigned to $cascade_status. The dead branch creates false confidence in a second defensive handler for SBP-CRIT-001's bypass path — no such handler exists.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:145 re.findall(r'^cascade-status:\\\\\\\\s+([a-z-]+)\\\\\\\\s*$', ...) — [a-z-]+ is strictly [a-z] and hyphen; space excluded. For 'cascade-status: not applicable', findall returns []; script exits 1 via set -e before reaching case. Lines 157-160 'not applicable') branch therefore never entered under any reachable execution path.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Apparent two-layer defense (first-pass early-exit + case branch) reduces to single layer. After SBP-CRIT-001 exploits the first-pass, the case branch provides no fallback. Code reviewers may incorrectly conclude a second handler closes the bypass surface, reducing urgency to fix SBP-CRIT-001.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Remove the unreachable 'not applicable') case branch (lines 157-160). After fixing SBP-CRIT-001, document that not-applicable detection is single-pass with strict line-start anchor. If defense-in-depth is desired, extend cascade_status regex to capture 'not applicable' as a valid multi-word value and re-add the case branch.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SBP-MIN-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"D-044 (docs/DECISIONS.md) describes 'cascade-status: not applicable → exit 0' without documenting the two-pass architecture or the leading-whitespace first-pass regex. An operator or auditor citing D-044 for safety properties of the not-applicable carve-out cannot discover the SBP-CRIT-001 bypass surface from the decision record alone.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"D-044 rationale states 'cascade-status: not applicable → exit 0' and 'exactly-one-match assertion (closes multi-occurrence injection bypass)'. No mention of dispatch_note_mode first pass, re.search first-match semantics, or ^[ \\\\\\\\t]* leading-whitespace tolerance. The exactly-one assertion claim is accurate for the second-pass enforcement but silent on the first-pass bypass surface.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Trust-model inaccuracy enables future operators to cite D-044 as evidence that not-applicable detection is secure, missing the leading-whitespace escape hatch. Adversarial review rounds citing D-044 for coverage of the multi-occurrence bypass may conclude the class is fully closed when SBP-CRIT-001 remains open.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Fix SBP-CRIT-001 (making D-044's implicit trust accurate by eliminating the bypass). Additionally amend D-044 to state that not-applicable detection uses a single strict-start-of-line regex, preventing future re-introduction of the leading-whitespace pattern as a silent regression.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SBP-MIN-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh has no regression test for DISPATCH-NOTE with '  cascade-status: not applicable' (indented, first occurrence) before 'cascade-status: onboarded'. Test case 14 confirms indented same-value duplicates are tolerated (exit 0) but does not guard the bypass class. SBP-CRIT-001 has no regression gate in the test suite.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"test case 14 DISPATCH-NOTE: '  cascade-status: onboarded\\\\\\\\ncascade-status: onboarded', expects exit 0 — confirming indented lines are tolerated. No test uses '  cascade-status: not applicable\\\\\\\\ncascade-status: onboarded'. Pre-fix this exits 0 (bypass); post-fix should exit non-zero (enforcement fires or dispatch_note_mode mismatch).\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"SBP-CRIT-001 fix can be silently re-introduced in a future refactor without test failure. CI gives false confidence that indented cascade-status variants are handled correctly for all combinations relevant to safety.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add test: DISPATCH-NOTE = '  cascade-status: not applicable\\\\\\\\ncascade-status: onboarded\\\\\\\\n- **Target:** jrnb2024/pim\\\\\\\\n' with branch-protection-log modified; expect non-zero exit after SBP-CRIT-001 fix. This test fails before fix (exposes the bypass) and passes after fix (proves regression guard active).\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SBP-nit-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"scaffold-downstream.sh lines 142-146: first case block denies /private/var/tmp|/private/var/tmp/* only. Second case block (lines 148-152) already covers /private/var|/private/var/* — a strict superset. The first block fires before the second but matches no path that the second does not also match; it is dead code with an identical die message.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"scaffold-downstream.sh:142-146 case $OUTPUT_DIR in /private/var/tmp|/private/var/tmp/*). Lines 148-152 include /private/var|/private/var/* which subsumes all /private/var/tmp/* paths. Both blocks emit identical error string. No path exists that matches the first block without matching the second.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Dead code; no functional security gap today. If the second case block is edited to carve out an exception for a /private/var/* subpath, the first block would silently fail to provide backup coverage for /private/var/tmp specifically.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Remove lines 142-146 (first case block). Consolidate all denylist patterns in the single second case block to eliminate maintenance divergence and the false layering impression.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SBP-nit-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"canonicalize_adopter_slug (lines 93-99) collapses dots and underscores to hyphens: 'org/repo.foo' and 'org/repo-foo' both yield 'org-repo-foo'. No runtime collision detection exists. A slug collision causes TF-024X-(renovate|conflict)-<slug> regex to match the wrong adopter's STATUS.md or DISPATCH-NOTE row, producing a false-positive pass.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Lines 95-98: re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9-]+', '-', s) normalises all non-[a-z0-9-] chars including dots and underscores to hyphens. 'jrnb2024/repo.foo' and 'jrnb2024/repo-foo' both yield 'jrnb2024-repo-foo'. Current 5-cohort repos (pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower) have no collisions. Plan-doc §2 states uniqueness-per-cohort but provides no runtime enforcement.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"False-positive TF row match for wrong adopter when slugs collide; STATUS.md check passes for adopter B because adopter A's correctly-formatted TF row matches the derived regex. Low risk for current fixed 5-cohort; elevated if cohort expands to repos with name variants.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Document the uniqueness precondition in the function header. For future cohort expansion, add a pre-authoring collision check validating no existing TF row in STATUS.md or branch-protection-log matches the new slug before onboarding proceeds.\\\"}]}\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"0453c3c1-f17c-4bb5-9675-6d7a022e5b3a\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.34960855,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":11,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":118765,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":650286,\"output_tokens\":47139,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":118765,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":3589,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":125549,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":597,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":597},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1886,\"outputTokens\":30,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.002036,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":11,\"outputTokens\":47139,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":650286,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":118765,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.34757255,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"36532a83-1729-4f8d-b030-62a270227105\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
