{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":436704,\"duration_api_ms\":437401,\"num_turns\":15,\"result\":\"All evidence collected. Composing the completeness governance review.\\n\\n{\\\"review_id\\\":\\\"r1-completeness_governance\\\",\\\"slice\\\":\\\"WP-SCP-024/024B-core\\\",\\\"lens\\\":\\\"completeness_governance\\\",\\\"reviewer\\\":\\\"sonnet-r1-completeness_governance\\\",\\\"date\\\":\\\"2026-05-09\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"CHANGES_REQUESTED\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"024B-core governance is substantially complete. SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md delivers rigorous empirical justification: R6→R7→R8 trajectory table, 3 enumerated structural problems, explicit incremental-not-descope framing, and extras-parking audit trail (7 fix-round logs + 7 R-round archives). D-044 is correctly scoped to core deliverables and cites SCOPE-CORRECTION by name. STATUS.md carries the PM chain entry with the split-decision operator record and extras-parking branch reference. Plan-doc §6 amendment correctly gates 024C on both halves plus FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001. Anti-descoping is preserved: neither half relaxes any invariant; extras-parking branch is intact with full audit trail. VERSIONING.md alignment confirmed: scaffolder, template, and CI script are all internal-only surfaces under VERSIONING.md §Scope — no version bump required. One MAJ: the scaffolder test suite does not verify the Renovate auto-bump marker passes through to emitted wrapper output. Plan-doc invariant 8 makes this marker the Threshold A Renovate mechanism; DISPATCH-NOTE AC #2 explicitly states it. The template carries the marker and sed passes it through unchanged — no code defect — but the absent test assertion means a future template edit could silently drop it without CI failure. Two MINs: stale 024B path in a code comment; STATUS.md row 3 parenthetical implies FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 was dropped when plan-doc §6 retains it. Cross-lens note: CORR-CRIT-001 (correctness lens) identifies an indented cascade-status bypass outside this lens's scope but must be resolved before fixpoint.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MAJ-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Scaffolder test suite asserts substitution, MANIFEST integrity, and wrapper contract properties but does not verify the Renovate auto-bump marker (# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-) is present in emitted wrapper output. DISPATCH-NOTE AC #2 explicitly names this marker; plan-doc invariant 8 makes it the Threshold A Renovate mechanism.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh:86-98 assert_wrapper_contract checks fork-PR refusal, least-privilege permissions, and absence of id-token/attestations — no grep for the Renovate marker. templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl:17 carries the marker. scaffold-downstream.sh:174-178 sed substitution passes static content through unchanged. main() at lines 120-123 checks branch/SHA/scorecard-emit but not the marker.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A future template edit removing the marker would not fail any test. Without the marker, cascade adopters receive no Renovate-driven SHA pin bumps, making Threshold A's Renovate-path criterion (plan-doc invariant 8, §8) structurally unachievable and every adopter permanently dependent on operator-driven R-024-07 fallback bumps.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add grep -Fq '# renovate: datasource=github-tags' \\\\\\\"$wrapper\\\\\\\" to assert_wrapper_contract. Single line; symmetric with the existing fork-PR refusal and permission checks already in the function.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh comment header (line 12) references docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md — the pre-split branch path. After the core/extras split the authoritative DISPATCH-NOTE is at docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md. This is a post-split artifact not cleaned up.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:12 — '# docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md; docs/DECISIONS.md D-044.' Actual DISPATCH-NOTE location: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md (per SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md §Reference and git status).\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Misleads maintainers about the authoritative DISPATCH-NOTE location. Not a functional defect. Risk grows as 024B-extras branch diverges and the bare 024B path may reference a different or absent file.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Update line 12 to reference docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"STATUS.md today's chain PM row 3 states '024C entry now conditional on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merged (was: 024B + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure)'. The parenthetical implies FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 was removed. The authoritative plan-doc §6 split note explicitly retains it: '024C remains gated on both halves merging, plus FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure'.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"STATUS.md:149 — 'now conditional on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merged (was: 024B + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure)'. docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:213 — 'plus FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure, before cohort onboarding opens'. DISPATCH-NOTE scope table: 'Plan-doc §6 amendment ... gates on BOTH halves merging + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001.'\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A 024C opener reading only STATUS.md could treat FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 as a retired gate and open the cascade prematurely. STATUS.md is what operators skim for current state; the authoritative plan-doc is correct but less visible.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Amend STATUS.md row 3 to clarify retention: e.g. '024C now gated on: (1) 024B-core merged, (2) 024B-extras merged, (3) FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closed (retained from pre-split gate).'\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-nit-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Plan-doc §6 slice ordering note reads '024B is a hard predecessor for 024C-024F' without post-split qualification. The adjacent 024B split note correctly states 'both halves merging' but the ordering note text itself does not reference the split, creating a fast-read ambiguity.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md line 215 (slice ordering note paragraph): '024B is a hard predecessor for 024C-024F (the scaffolder must exist before any cascade slice can use it).' Adjacent split note at line 213 provides the correct 'both halves' gate language.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Cosmetic; correct information is nearby. A fast reader could incorrectly conclude 024B-core alone (without extras) is sufficient to open 024C.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Change '024B is a hard predecessor' to '024B-core + 024B-extras (both required) are hard predecessors' in the slice ordering note.\\\"}]}\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"7c2a20a0-caa3-46b6-a68f-89cec26b5eb1\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.0054157,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":118736,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":496029,\"output_tokens\":27315,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":118736,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":2426,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":118080,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":8037,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":8037},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1482,\"outputTokens\":22,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001592,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":10,\"outputTokens\":27315,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":496029,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":118736,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.0038236999999999,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"a0281c6b-b670-448d-8893-e366dc928343\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
